From cbdf2fba5b11d1e7bc9a9f5b495c502a64fc6574 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:29:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 064/130] render: preprocess shaders by WE's rules, and compile
 them with HLSL's
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WE turns its GLSL-dialect shaders into HLSL and hands them to D3DCompile (wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485: the include
pass GH 0x140191050 / 0x1401917f0, the translator GH 0x140125e80, the compile GH 0x140106780 with flags 0x8800);
LWE handed them to glslang as GLSL 3.30 with its own include placement and a few ad-hoc retries, and 21 of the
library's 96 scenes lost layers or effects to shaders WE builds. Now (WEShaderRules, ShaderUnit, GLSLContext):

- WE's rules: an include is pasted where its line is, and only a line starting `#include` is one (was: all
  before main, commented ones too — 3235948233's auto_sway, M_PI above main); declarations are hoisted ahead of
  the code as WE's cbuffers/structs are (an include sees the unit's uniforms); the fragment's varyings take the
  vertex unit's types (WE's PS input is the VS_OUTPUT; a vec2-in/vec4-out pair got NVIDIA C7011); a fragment's
  varyings and a vertex's attributes are writable, the copy filled in every main (only the first was: auto_sway's
  active main read v_TexCoord 0, so 3414858021's 左白巾 vanished when it compiled); declared gl_ built-ins dropped;
  WE's header macros (CASTF/I/U, CAST4U, the sampler parameter macros, texLoad2D, texSample2DCompare, the frame
  buffer mappings) and the HLSL type names; an #if a preprocessor can't read is false; formatcombo samplers get
  TEX<n>FORMAT.
- HLSL's semantics, from glslang's errors: assignments and call arguments convert (truncate, promote, change
  base), operands truncate (the identifier picked by the error's storage, never a declared name), a scalar is a
  condition, a local const takes any initializer and a global one is a static const set in main, a function with
  no return on the combo's path returns zero, GLSL-reserved names (`input`) are renamed, a user function overloading
  an intrinsic the header has as a macro (log10) gets real overloads, clip() exists.
- Inferred (not read in WE's code): a missing uniform default / short vector default is zero; include-once.

The shader sweep: 4085 compiles of WE's 124 stock shaders and the library's 272 custom ones, 313 failed in 35
shaders before, see docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "Shader preprocessing result".

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/reports/scene-health.md (shader errors WE accepts) and the sweep
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
